// Port Oakes


// HISTORY

// Eldritch War

"CoTHistory2" "Long ago, a group of cultists called the 'Children of Enos' fled France and settled in these isles. French accounts claim the cultists practiced dark rituals, human sacrifice, and the summoning of demons. They were eventually defeated by a team of heroes led by the famous Father Martin Henri."

// Swashbuckler
"PirateHistory4" "Blackbeard himself captured this fort in 1718. He tortured and killed the ill-prepared French soldiers manning it, leaving behind legends of ghostly hauntings that still persist to this day. Father Martin Henri, a famous adventurer of the Rogue Isles, is said to have hallowed the fort by day, but there are rumors that the spirits return to the fort by night."


//TOURISM

// Scurvy Dog
"PortOakes1" "The owner of Blackbeard's pub is rumored to have sent more than one patron to Davey Jones' locker."

// Washed Up
"PortOakes2" "Emil Marcone's brother was found at low-tide in this particular vehicle."

// Powder Monkey
"PortOakes3" "The last of the pirates died at this location defending the fort against Blackbeard."

// Driller
"PortOakes4" "Three years ago, Ms. Liberty smashed the supervillian Thermonuke through the deck and into the volatile crude below. Thermonuke's devastating powers ignited the oil and cracked open the Cairo Queen like a pixie stick."


